                "text": "We need construct 3 demo pairs. Need call show_transformed_input with inputs. Need ensure valid and varied. The rule is deterministic. We can create 10x10 grids with column0 colored values. Need 3 examples.\n\nWe want teach Student. Since Student sees only pairs, we should include all four colors across examples ideally, varied rows, maybe repeats, empty rows. We need use tool calls. We can submit one at a time or multiple in parallel? Tool calls independent. But show_transformed_input returns output. We can call multiple in one block. Need provide input grids.\n\nLet's design three 10x10 input grids.\n\nExample 1: include all colors in column0 and some empty rows.\nRows 0-9:\n[8,0...], [2,...], [4,...], [3,...], [0...], [8...], [0...], [4...], [2...], [3...]\nAll other columns 0.\nVerifier will map.\n\nExample 2: different arrangement, maybe all four colors reversed, some columns 0 only. Ensure input values in column0 only; verifier ignores other columns. But to be clean, all zeros except col0.\n\nExample 3: more rows, include zeros. We can also include colors with repeats and empty rows.\n\nNeed 10x10 rectangular. Let's define.\n\nInput1:\nrow0 [8,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0]\nrow1 [2,0,...]\nrow2 [4,...]\nrow3 [3,...]\nrow4 zeros\nrow5 [3,...]\nrow6 [0,...]\nrow7 [8,...]\nrow8 [2,...]\nrow9 [4,...]\n\nOutputs: row0 col1=8; row1 col2=2; row2 col3=4; row3 col4=3; row4 zeros; row5 col4=3; row6 zeros; row7 col1=8; row8 col2=2; row9 col3=4.\n\nInput2 maybe:\nzeros, [3], [4], [2], [8], zeros, [2], [3], [8], [4]\nInclude all.\n\nInput3:\n[4], [3], [8], [2], [0], [0], [4], [2], [3], [8]\nMaybe.\n\nNeed call show_transformed_input. It will compute. Let's do three calls in parallel. Wait if parallel, response returns outputs. Fine.\n\nNeed be careful JSON format. Use arrays.\n\nLet's call.",
